    "notes": "negative offer ids in their canonical int64 spelling, as text (-1, -16, -9223372036854775808) and as JSON numbers (-1, -16). offerID is an int64 in ManageSellOfferOp and ManageBuyOfferOp, and SEP-51 writes an int64 as a base-10 decimal string, so each input is the exact rendering of a value the XDR type holds; an XDR-JSON reader that reads the type encodes it as written. core refuses the operation with MANAGE_SELL_OFFER_MALFORMED / MANAGE_BUY_OFFER_MALFORMED for offerID < 0 from protocol 15 (stellar-core v30.0.0 src/transactions/ManageOfferOpFrameBase.cpp, ManageOfferOpFrameBase::doCheckValid), so an API that builds operations and applies that rule refuses it. each case expects either the exact id, carried in a ManageSellOfferOp, or a refusal (negative); encoding any other id fails. -0 is not the canonical spelling of 0 and stays in the non-canonical entry.",
